The attached image (Figure 4) illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are actively transported by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) to the draining lymph nodes over time. Flow cytometry plots and associated bar charts demonstrate the detection and phenotyping of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells, distinguishing between migratory dendritic cells (MigDC), lymphoid tissue resident dendritic cells (LTDC), and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ). The percentage of Nano-11-containing cells in the draining lymph node peaks around Day 2, with MigDCs being the predominant subtype. Furthermore, MigDCs show the highest mean fluorescence intensity, indicating greater per-cell uptake of Nano-11 compared to other APCs.